WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.030
A mountain's height is only the visible part of the story.

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:09.090
Beneath a major mountain belt, thick, relatively buoyant crust extends downward

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:13.430
as a root. Isostasy describes how regional elevation adjusts to the

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.310
types and thicknesses of rock below.

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:19.550
Continental crust is commonly thirty to fifty kilometers thick, compared with

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:22.090
roughly seven kilometers for oceanic crust.

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:25.370
Those are typical values, not measurements of every location.

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:27.640
Thickness is not the only control.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.880
With similar crustal thickness, less dense material supports higher elevation.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.740
Heating expands rock and lowers its density, so regional heating can

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:38.380
cause uplift. Cooling has the opposite effect.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:40.760
The mantle here remains predominantly solid:

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:44.280
warmth and slow deformation do not mean a worldwide ocean of

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:44.720
magma.

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:48.050
Compression folds and thrusts the crust, making it thicker.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:52.090
Extension stretches it and moves blocks along normal faults, making it

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:57.410
thinner. Erosion removes material; deposition and volcanic eruptions add material at

00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:01.630
the surface. Intruding magma adds material at depth and also transfers

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:04.690
heat. A surface load can build up the ground while pushing

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:08.550
the underlying crust downward. Several mechanisms can operate together.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:12.440
Keep crustal thickness separate from lithospheric thickness.

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:15.560
The lithosphere includes crust and rigid upper mantle.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:19.180
As an oceanic plate moves away from a ridge, it cools,

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:22.440
its mantle lithosphere thickens, and the plate subsides.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:27.980
Replacing dense continental mantle lithosphere with warmer asthenosphere can instead raise

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:30.040
a region, even without thickening its crust.

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:34.670
The historical clue was a surveying discrepancy near the Himalaya.

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:38.430
A hanging weight leaned toward the mountains, but less than expected.

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:43.290
A deep root of lower-density crust displaces denser mantle, reducing the

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:48.290
predicted attraction. The iceberg analogy helps explain buoyancy, but the supporting

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:53.110
mantle is solid rock. To explain elevation, ask what changed in

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:55.590
thickness, density, temperature, and load.
